  "final_message": "`reports.mrr` returned negative totals because it subtracted each subscription's monthly amount from zero instead of adding it. With your example (30.00 USD monthly, 120.00 USD yearly), it reported -40.00 USD instead of 40.00 USD.\n\n**Fix:** in `billing/reports.py`, `mrr()` now adds `monthly_amount(...)` to the running total instead of subtracting it. The yearly normalisation in `monthly_amount` was already correct (12000 / 12 = 1000 cents).\n\n**Verification:**\n- I added `tests/test_reports.py`, which mixes a monthly subscription (3 \u00d7 10.00) and a yearly one (120.00) and expects `{\"usd\": 4000}`. It failed with `{'usd': -4000}` before the fix.\n- After the fix, the full suite passes: 25 passed, including the new test.\n\n**`answer.json`** in the repo root:\n```json\n{\"file\": \"reports.py\", \"function\": \"mrr\"}\n```\n\nI did not commit anything.",
